  <Properties>
    <metaDescription>
      <Value><![CDATA[This year’s Umbraco Winter Keynote has just dropped, and in this post we summarise the main points of interest.]]></Value>
    </metaDescription>
    <metaTitle>
      <Value><![CDATA[Umbraco Update: Product and strategy highlights from the Winter Keynote]]></Value>
    </metaTitle>
    <openGraphImage>
      <Value><![CDATA[]]></Value>
    </openGraphImage>
    <pageContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a58b29f0-29c6-47b8-b8ce-329b38fbed3c",
      "key": "2b3c4d5e-6f7a-8b9c-1d2e-3f4a5b6c7d8e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "<h3>Improved support from Umbraco HQ</h3><p>Persson also announced a number of improvements to Umbraco HQ support, including a 24/7 offering, a new Partner Portal, and a new 100% target in Umbraco’s SLA.</p><h3>ISO 27001 certification now achieved</h3><p>Umbraco’s ISO 27001 certification has now been achieved. This is a significant step that will tick a box for many IT buyers and help Umbraco win larger and more complex organisations.</p><h3>Umbraco's AI Strategy</h3><p>AI is everywhere, and a significant proportion of the session focused on Umbraco’s AI strategy, and a current and upcoming set of capabilities that support AI both inside and beyond Umbraco.</p><h3>Umbraco Compose and Enterprise</h3><p>Umbraco Compose was announced as a data orchestration platform, alongside details on the new Umbraco for Enterprise offering.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
